  data:  # b3ec
    kind: work_item  # b3ec
    title: "Framework-dispatch linkers (jackson/kafka_streams/view_template/react_component) must traverse transitive base-class hierarchy"  # b3ec
    status: todo_hard  # b3ec
    priority: 2  # b3ec
    parent:  # b3ec
    tags: []  # b3ec
    isbefore: []  # b3ec
    duplicate_of: []  # b3ec
    not_duplicate_of: []  # b3ec
    pr_ref:  # b3ec
    description: "## Origin\n\nCross-language framework-dispatch linker survey 2026-05-07, conducted as a structural-fix scope-expansion question following WI-halat (PR #3539, commit 0553b699f). WI-halat fixed the direct-only-base-match gap in `airflow_framework_dispatch.py` and `django_orm_dispatch.py` by wiring them through the new shared `linkers/_transitive_bases.py` helper (BFS over extends/implements edges with cycle guard). The survey asked: do other framework-dispatch linkers exhibit the same gap?\n\nAnswer: yes, in four within-language linkers. Each one matches against `meta.base_classes` directly without walking edges to transitive ancestors, so a class that extends an intermediate (project-defined or framework-provided) before reaching the framework's actual base never matches.\n\n## Affected linkers (4)\n\n1. **`linkers/jackson_dispatch.py`** (Java/Kotlin/Scala — Jackson, JPA, Spring): line 184 reads `base_classes = sym.meta.get(\"base_classes\")` and iterates the direct list only. Spring + JPA layered hierarchies are the dominant pattern (`@MappedSuperclass` → `@Entity`); WI-sokaz already inferred this without explicitly fixing the traversal. **Highest-ROI target** — could regression-cap WI-sokaz's spring-petclinic UAT re-validation if shipped without this.\n\n2. **`linkers/kafka_streams_dispatch.py`** (Java/Kotlin/Scala — Kafka Streams: Processor, Transformer, ValueMapper, Merger): line 147 iterates `(\"base_classes\", \"interfaces\")` direct only. Kotlin/Scala wrappers around Java SAM types are a common nesting pattern.\n\n3. **`linkers/view_template.py`** (Ruby — Rails: ApplicationController, ActionController::Base/API): lines 196 + 288 use `for base in base_classes` direct only. Rails projects ubiquitously subclass a project-defined `ApplicationController` (intermediate above `ActionController::Base`).\n\n4. **`linkers/react_component.py`** (JS/TS — React class components): matches `React.Component` / `PureComponent` only as direct `base_classes` entry. Class components are mostly legacy in React 16+; gap exists structurally but real-world impact is mild.\n\n## Fix scope (option (a) per WI-halat)\n\nPer-linker walk via the existing helper:\n\n```python\nfrom .._transitive_bases import build_inheritance_index, collect_transitive_base_names\n\n# in the linker's run() method, once per pass:\ninheritance_index = build_inheritance_index(edges)\n\n# at the per-class match site:\ncandidate_bases = collect_transitive_base_names(class_sym, symbol_by_id, inheritance_index)\nif FRAMEWORK_BASE_NAMES & set(candidate_bases):\n    ...\n```\n\nMechanical change — ~5-10 LOC per linker. Each linker also needs:\n- Property test: one- and two-intermediate transitive chains pass; diamond-inheritance cycle is guarded.\n- Direct-base regression guard: existing direct-match cases continue to work.\n\nEstimate ~1-2 days total across the four linkers.\n\n## Why option (a) and not option (b)\n\nOption (b) — transitively close `meta.base_classes` in every language analyzer pre-emit — was rejected at WI-halat time because the cost is much higher (touches every analyzer, wide-blast-radius behavioral change, requires coordinated SCHEMA bump). The four-linker per-consumer fix delivers the same observable behavior at a fraction of the cost. If a fifth or sixth gap surfaces later, revisit option (b) at that point.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- New property tests in each of the four linkers' test files cover (1) one-intermediate chain, (2) two-intermediate chain, (3) diamond-inheritance cycle, (4) direct-base regression.\n- Each linker's existing tests still pass.\n- 100% coverage on changed sources.\n\n## UAT validation expectations\n\n- **jackson_dispatch**: Spring + JPA monorepo — `@Entity` accessors via intermediate `@MappedSuperclass` chains receive `dispatches_to` edges. Could ride alongside the WI-sokaz spring-petclinic re-run.\n- **kafka_streams_dispatch**: Kafka Streams app with Kotlin/Scala wrapper layers — Processor/Transformer/ValueMapper/Merger overrides via intermediate base classes detected.\n- **view_template**: Rails app with project-internal `ApplicationController` extending `ActionController::Base` — controller actions detected through the intermediate.\n- **react_component**: legacy React class-component repo with project-internal `BaseComponent extends React.Component` — render/lifecycle overrides detected.\n\n## Cross-references\n\n- WI-halat (done, P2): the original Python-only fix that introduced `_transitive_bases.py`.\n- WI-sokaz (done, P2): jackson_dispatch JPA annotation extension; this item is the orthogonal traversal fix that protects WI-sokaz's UAT re-validation.\n- WI-likab linkage **refuted**: WI-halat author noted the Go access_mode cap is a Tier 1 dataflow propagation issue, not a base-class traversal gap.\n- INV-vusog: about *emitting* one-hop extends/implements edges from `meta.base_classes` — the substrate this work consumes; out of scope.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- The Go grpc.py struct-embedding traversal gap — separate item.\n- The type_hierarchy.py skip-level dispatches_to gap — different shape, separate item.\n- Option (b) analyzer-side transitive closure of `meta.base_classes` — explicitly deferred unless additional gaps surface."  # b3ec
    fields: {}  # b3ec
